      "sequence_position": 10,
      "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,-2 & 4 \\\\ \\,2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrix $A$ above, evaluate the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}^{T}\\,Ay$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain   \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ay \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =28.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
